{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix pushed — Gerrit change 2345\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2345 — `Run sync MCP tool bodies off the loop`\n(commit bfe69394b11d, branch reb-d240-mcp-init-cold-start off origin/main b75bf4bc0951).\n\nTwo files, exactly as declared in file_impact:\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — `_thread_offloaded` + `offload_sync_tools`, wired from\n  `wire_health` AFTER `instrument_certified_tools`; `InFlightGauge`'s docstring corrected\n  (its stated premise, that track runs on the event-loop thread, no longer holds).\n  372 -> 463 lines, within the 800 cap.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_tool_offload.py` — new, 8 tests.\n\n### RED-first, mutation-checked\n\nRED before the fix (ImportError: `offload_sync_tools` does not exist). GREEN after: 8/8.\n\nMutation check — the symbol kept, the behaviour removed (`tool.fn`/`tool.is_async`\nassignments replaced by a bare counter increment). **4 of 8 tests went RED, each for the\nright reason:**\n\n    test_a_slow_sync_tool_does_not_block_concurrent_work\n      AssertionError: the event loop was occupied by the sync tool body, so no other\n      request could be served while it ran\n    test_a_sync_tool_body_runs_off_the_event_loop_thread\n      AssertionError: assert 'MainThread' != 'MainThread'\n    test_certified_tools_keep_their_gauge_instrumentation_after_the_offload\n      assert 0 == 1        (the gauge watcher never got scheduled)\n    test_the_offload_reports_how_many_tools_it_moved\n      assert 1 == 0\n\nThe core test asserts a VALUE, not a duration: the tool body waits on a\n`threading.Event` that only a concurrently-scheduled coroutine can set, so it reports\n\"released\" when the loop is free and \"blocked\" when it is not. Deterministic in what it\nproves; no wall-clock threshold to go flaky.\n\n### Gates\n\n    plan-review        PASS, signed, 0 blocking / 0 advisory / 0 indeterminate\n    make lint          pass (ruff check + format-check, shellcheck, zizmor)\n    make typecheck     Success: no issues found in 683 source files\n    module-size gate   4 passed (_mcp_health.py 463 lines)\n    complexity ratchet active=39 new=0 increased=0 stale=10\n    regression sweep   504 passed, 9 skipped (-k \"mcp or health or opcert or cross_session\")\n\n### Not closing this ticket\n\nAC 4 requires live validation against the deployed server after the change lands, and the\nchange is not yet merged (`Verified +1` / `LLM-Review +1` pending). Per AGENTS.md a ticket\ndoes not close before its change is green in CI and merged.\n\n### Follow-up filed\n\n`vaccinated-flavorous-solenodon` (e1d9-4c8e-3fd1-41c2), linked `discovered_from` this\nticket: /health cannot see the MCP request path, so the blue-green cutover promotes a\ncontainer that has never served one. Real, cited, and separate from this root cause — and\nit should follow this fix, because while sync tool bodies occupied the event loop /health\nwas unanswerable during any long tool call anyway."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787953632117315001,"uuid":"2a8b6fa4-802e-4b7e-b4f9-55fdd1ac572f"}